{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01T4Pr4jVj8ktUPpUzNGe88f","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"answer\\\":\\\"Based on my search of the context filesystem, I found the answer in the KIP-1312 discussion thread.\\\\n\\\\n## Answer\\\\n\\\\nThe error code name returned when a client tries to unregister a controller ID that has no existing registration is:\\\\n\\\\n**`CONTROLLER_ID_NOT_REGISTERED`**\\\\n\\\\n### Citation\\\\n\\\\nThis error code was discussed and agreed upon in the KIP-1312 \\\\\\\"Support unregistering controllers\\\\\\\" thread. Jun Rao explicitly proposed this error code in his response:\\\\n\\\\n> \\\\\\\"Another way is to introduce a new CONTROLLER_ID_NOT_REGISTERED error code.\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\nThis is documented in: **`_intake/2026/05/12/mail-f884fe02638d7de53fef380a-24f3c9a1.md`** (Message from Jun Rao via dev, May 12, 2026)\\\\n\\\\nKevin Wu confirmed this in his reply:\\\\n\\\\n> \\\\\\\"I like the idea of a separate `CONTROLLER_ID_NOT_REGISTERED` error code for unregistering a controller which is not registered. I have updated the KIP with this.\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\nThis is documented in: **`_intake/2026/05/12/mail-1736e3e8f4a1ef534d61f830-daf404c7.md`** (Message from Kevin Wu, May 12, 2026)\\\",\\\"error\\\":null,\\\"files\\\":[\\\"store\\\",\\\"_intake/2026/04/02/mail-7f1f1872d11282867712a8ad-aafee31a.md\\\",\\\"kips/KIP-1282.md\\\",\\\"kips/kip-1191.md\\\",\\\"_intake/2026/04/03/mail-5bf246535561f045598ad4c1-7696291b.md\\\",\\\"_intake/2026/04/20/mail-12165bf3fba14415eca7bb84-52b55e7d.md\\\",\\\"_intake/2026/04/21/mail-7339fe22b599504717ee7b74-daa8a13c.md\\\",\\\"pull-requests/pr-21312.md\\\",\\\"_intake/2026/04/24/mail-16dc98c0275f2390362a36bc-ba70833d.md\\\",\\\"_intake/2026/04/10/github-api-apache-kafka-review-comment-PRRC_kwDOACG9q862mmA0-131271fc.md\\\",\\\"_intake/2026/04/27/mail-1e8033852f224df1ee0e36b2-f8b6b2aa.md\\\",\\\"_intake/2026/05/12/mail-1736e3e8f4a1ef534d61f830-daf404c7.md\